{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"2238","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"B. Crimson Triples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"1 second"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Chills run down your spine..."}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"— Terraria"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"After summoning the next boss — The Brain of Cthulhu, you noticed that it surrounds itself with $$$n$$$ eyes, numbered from $$$1$$$ to $$$n$$$. In one attack, The Brain of Cthulhu chooses a triple of eyes (not necessarily distinct) with numbers $$$(a, b, c)$$$. The triple of eyes is called "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"crimson"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" if and only if the following property holds: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$\\gcd$$$$$$^{\\text{∗}}$$$$$$(\\operatorname{lcm}$$$$$$^{\\text{†}}$$$$$$(a, b), \\operatorname{lcm}(b, c)) = \\gcd(a, c)$$$, "}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"To defeat the boss, you want to know how many ways The Brain of Cthulhu can choose a crimson triple of eyes. The triples of eyes $$$(a_1, b_1, c_1)$$$ and $$$(a_2, b_2, c_2)$$$ are considered different if $$$a_1 \\neq a_2$$$, or $$$b_1 \\neq b_2$$$, or $$$c_1 \\neq c_2$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"$$$^{\\text{∗}}$$$$$$\\gcd(x, y)$$$ denotes the "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Greatest_common_divisor"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"greatest common divisor (GCD)"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":" of integers $$$x$$$ and $$$y$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"$$$^{\\text{†}}$$$$$$\\operatorname{lcm}(x, y)$$$ denotes the "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Least_common_multiple"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"least common multiple (LCM)"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":" of integers $$$x$$$ and $$$y$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Each test contains multiple test cases. The first line contains the number of test cases $$$t$$$ ($$$1 \\le t \\le 1000$$$). The description of the test cases follows."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The only line of each test case contains one integer $$$n$$$ ($$$1 \\le n \\le 2 \\cdot 10^5$$$) — the number of eyes of The Brain of Cthulhu."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It is guaranteed that the sum of $$$n$$$ across all test cases does not exceed $$$2 \\cdot 10^5$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each test case, output one integer — the number of ways to choose a crimson triple of eyes."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n3\n1\n2\n20\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n1\n5\n612\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first test case, there is $$$1$$$ possible crimson triple: $$$(1, 1, 1)$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second test case, there are $$$5$$$ possible crimson triples: $$$(1, 1, 1)$$$, $$$(1, 1, 2)$$$, $$$(2, 1, 1)$$$, $$$(2, 1, 2)$$$, $$$(2, 2, 2)$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"B","problemCode":"2238B","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/2238/problem/B"}